A first-person age under 18 in the text (first_person_minors). It
    only adds caution, never removes it:

    - a cast member who says it ("LILY: I'm nine") is a minor now, in
      every part;
    - the narrator, when the facts reply says they are a minor now, stays
      one (in every part);
    - the narrator, when the reply gives them an adult age (18 or over):
      shown as a minor in each part whose own words say it (part-local;
      not carried to later parts: the reply's own minor_in_past /
      in_this_part / minor_when say the rest), with the scene rule;
    - the narrator, when the reply misses them, says unknown, or gives no
      adult age: a minor now, in every part.

Clip check (services/inspector.py): each new storyboard clip is looked at
by a vision model (mock here) and the verdict is kept on its take.

- frames are pulled from the clip (4, spread out, edges skipped, ≤ 512 px);
- the verdict is stored on the take and exposed on ShotOut, the takes list
  and the render plan ("2 clips flagged by the check");
- a refusal / DECLINED / garbage reply is "unsure", never "problem";
- the automatic check is skipped when switched off, noted when over the
  monthly budget; the manual check is guarded like any paid call;
- a failing check never touches the render;
- migration 0007.

Follow-ups to the "don't waste paid work" changes:

- a video job whose download was interrupted (stuck in "completing") stops
  counting as being made, and the sweeper fails it;
- Retry on a project rendered before voiceover fingerprints existed reuses
  the voiceover instead of buying it again;
- an empty spoken script renders without a voice instead of failing;
- a lip-synced shot is not re-rolled against an out-of-date voiceover;
- re-plan with "keep my edits" never makes a finished clip out of date;
- the ambient picture is made in the first variation's light;
- resuming an ambient loop keeps the model the kept clips were made with.

Follow-ups to the clean-deployment checks (ADULT_FEATURES=false), each
with the default (adult features on) case unchanged:

1. an avoid list that asks for explicit content is refused (OpenRouter sends
   it inside the prompt text), while one that only names what to keep out
   is not;
2. music and nature-sound prompts get the explicit-content check before the
   provider is paid;
3. known DeepSeek derivatives under other names can't be the planner;
4. a voiceover uploaded before the switch is refused by every way a video
   is recomposed (Retry, re-rolls, the worker itself);
5. an ambient loop checks every prompt it will send before the first paid
   call, in the API and in the worker;
6. a lip-sync's motion and script are each judged once.

Storyboard editing basics:

- hear the voiceover before paying for video (and the next render reuses
  it at no charge), with the project's own voice;
- add, duplicate and delete shots by hand;
- keep earlier takes of a shot and pick one again without paying;
- change project settings after creation (aspect ratio remakes clips,
  caption style only needs a re-compose);
- migration 0006.

Storyboard renders must not waste money or silently lose work:

- a failed voiceover stops the render before any clip is submitted;
- an edited shot gets a new clip (and says so before the render);
- an unchanged voiceover is reused, a changed one is made new;
- a clip still being made is never submitted a second time;
- re-plan with "keep my edits" keeps the edited script, end card, captions
  and each shot's avoid text.

